# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cochange_store.py" "CO-CHANGE STORE GATE: PASS" "co-change store (cache + ingest + partner read, moat-isolated)" "co-change store: turns the _cg_cochange extractor into a live, per-tenant, content-free signal. (1) ingest_cochange_with_authority stores a repo's co-change pairs through the gated write path (governed-write forgery gate, FORCE RLS); (2) co_change_partners_with_authority returns the 'you touched A; B historically comes with it' hint ranked by LIFT (base-rate-corrected: how many times more than chance) with the directional CONFIDENCE for the human display -- never a raw count, never an average; (3) MOAT: a SECOND tenant reading the SAME repo coordinate sees NOTHING (the co-change cache is FORCE-RLS-walled per account exactly like the code graph -- co-change must not leak across tenants); (4) re-ingest is idempotent (DELETE+reINSERT -- a derived cache); (5) content-free throughout (paths + counts only, no commit message / file body / author / SHA). The read fn re-pins current_account from the session identity (enter_installation sets it txn-local) exactly as main_impact_surface does. content-free + precision-disciplined (lift drops a hot file that co-changes with everything; support floor drops coincidences; giant commits skipped)" "co-change store: per-tenant content-free co-change cache + gated ingest + lift-ranked partner read, moat-isolated (a 2nd tenant sees nothing); the empirical coupling signal is now persistable + queryable per repo" 24
